@title Staff Password and MFA FAQ
@subtitle Cinder Valley School District IT, policy effective 2026-11-03

This page answers the most common questions about the new password and multi-factor authentication policy for staff accounts. Read it before November 3, and send anything it does not cover to the help desk.

!! IT will never ask for your password or your code by email or phone.

## Why are we changing the policy?

Two phishing incidents in 2026 compromised staff mailboxes. Longer passwords and multi-factor authentication stop that kind of attack.

## What changes on November 3?

Passwords must be at least 14 characters long, and every staff account needs multi-factor authentication.

## Do I have to change my password every 90 days?

No. We are removing forced rotation. We will only ask you to change your password after a suspected compromise.

## What if I do not have a smartphone?

The help desk will issue a hardware key at no cost.

## What if I lose my phone or key?

Call the help desk at extension 4400. They will issue a temporary bypass code valid for 24 hours.

## Who do I contact for help?

The help desk, open 07:00 to 17:00 on school days.
